A||||4||Black86SE||Pulling engine||||1||
Z||000000||Black86SE||10-15-2001||12:01 AM||||I plan on pulling my engine this winter and painting it and cleaning everything up. Maybe installing a 5-speed and getting rid of my auto. Anything I should be wary of when I am doing this? Any tips?<P>How about colors? What color(s) should I paint things? Thanks for the info.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2_4.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>1986 V6 SE<BR>Black<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||12:31 AM||||You're biggest problem is proabably going to be stuck bolts.<BR>As for the color, I suggest a metallic grey. <p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pike||10-15-2001||01:10 AM||||Pulling the pallet is a lot of work...are you sure you want to go through it just for paint? Your engine pic looks pretty good to me as-is! Why not just do a good steam-clean on it and call it good...unless you have major engine work to do...<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||10-15-2001||01:34 AM||||as far as wiring - the easist way is to detach the wiring inside the car and remove it through the bulk head, then all wiring will be free and clear as you remove the sub-frame<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||88Style||10-15-2001||11:53 AM||||This is correct. Don't disconnect all the different connectors from the engine to pull it. The book suggested this and I did it only to find out later that they can be removed from the computer. As far as anything else.. have handy shallow sockets, deep sockets and wrenches in the following sizes. 10mm, 13mm, 15mm, and 18mm. Also consider buying an 18mm impact socket. I broke two regular sockets trying to remove the cradle bolts. <P>||||reg||1
